-- title:
--   Base change of the X_H(M) q-expansion field is a curve over L
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a perfect field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure (so of characteristic zero), let $M$ be a natural number with $M \neq 0$, and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M\mathbb{Z})^{\times}$. Write $F_0 =$ `xHFunctionField M H`, the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq F_0 \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ given by `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)`, and let $F =$ `laurentBaseChange L F₀` be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise ring map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. The theorem asserts two things about $F$ as an extension of $L$. First, `IsCurveOver L F`: every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a divisor $D$ of degree $0$ with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$ of $F/L$ (a place being a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $L$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring); each such place has residue field finite as an $L$-module; and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega[F⁄L]$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$. Second, `Algebra.EssFiniteType L F`.
--
--   Classically this says that the field of modular functions for $\Gamma_H(M)$, with coefficients extended to $L$, is a function field of one variable over $L$ in the structural sense used in this development (principal divisors of degree zero, finite residue extensions, one-dimensional space of differentials). It supplies the standing curve hypotheses for the divisor, Riemann–Roch and automorphism results about $X_H(M)$ and its base changes, in particular over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isCurveOver_and_essFiniteType_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField.lean

